  updated="2026-09-30"
>
  <p slot="intro" class="guide-intro">Cum laude, magna cum laude and summa cum laude are Latin honors: distinctions a college adds to a degree for high grades. Summa cum laude is the highest. Each college sets its own rules: at the five colleges compared below, cum laude takes a GPA of 3.2 to 3.5, magna cum laude 3.5 to 3.75 and summa cum laude 3.8 to 3.95. To see where you stand, use the <a href="/gpa-calculator/">GPA calculator</a>.</p>

